# Format D: story/cutscene text (renderer C2:0F63 typewriter, C2:0EBF instant). One byte per 16x16 glyph.
# Font: 160 glyphs, 2bpp, 4 tiles each (TL TR BL BR), raw at file 0x41000 (DMA'd to VRAM $4000); tile = code*4 + base.
# Each string starts with a 4-byte header (speed, x, y, attr) that the extractor keeps apart; see docs/re/text.md.
# Read off the font sheet (work/re/glyphs16.py 41000 160), checked against the story pages in clear_3.
